      <documentation>Usually fails straight away, without asking the bank: ApiKit itself decides this SCA (it verifies the TAN it collected), so a bank-side status could only contradict a verification that never happened. The exception is a decoupled SCA method selected inside this approach - from there the bank runs the SCA and owns its outcome, exactly as in the pure-decoupled flow. Which of the two it is cannot be told from the approach, since selecting a method does not change it; the gateway behind this timer asks the SCA method instead. Interrupting: the interactive part is torn down before the timeout decides, so no second token can finalise behind our back.</documentation>
